  "description_short": "Family-run seafood spot in Sedgefield serving fresh linefish, calamari, and generous portions at honest prices.",
  "description_long": "Tucked into Sedgefield's business centre along Main Service Road, The Captain's Cook has built a loyal following for straightforward, well-executed seafood. This is the kind of place where locals pop in for midweek fish and chips or a proper linefish braai, knowing they'll get quality without fuss.\n\nThe menu keeps things simple: fresh catch of the day, golden calamari, prawns done just right, and chips that actually taste like potatoes. Portions are generous, prices are fair, and the kitchen doesn't try to be fancy — just good seafood cooked well. It's the sort of neighbourhood spot that gets the basics right, which in a town like Sedgefield means everything.\n\nThe setting is casual and unpretentious, perfect for families stopping through or locals grabbing takeaways. With its solid 4.5-star rating built on consistent quality rather than hype, The Captain's Cook proves you don't need ocean views to serve honest, satisfying seafood on the Garden Route.",
